module Innate;
profile Core;

// The compiler's innate concepts: rules every Concept program satisfies,
// written in Concept and applied by the compiler to every declaration of
// their kind. No program can omit, weaken, or redefine them.
//
// This module ships inside the compiler. Its source hash is the innate
// identity recorded in every semantic module artifact.
// See docs/design/EVT2-INNATE-CONCEPTS.md.

// The result of an innate predicate. Refuted names the declaration the
// diagnostic points at, and a message that says what is wrong and how to fix
// it. The compiler relies on this exact shape.
enum Verdict
{
    Holds,
    Refuted(declaration at, string message),
}
